//? Title: Causal attention with padded sequences
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Run causal self-attention on a batch with valid sequence lengths 5, 3 and 0.
Inspect the masked probabilities, verify that padded inputs and outputs have
zero gradients, and compare all 120 input derivatives against finite differences.
)

> Why mask both query and key positions?

An autoregressive query at position i can attend to key positions through i.
When batches are padded to a common width, a padding mask must also exclude
invalid keys and disable queries whose positions are themselves padding.
For sequence length L, a pair (i, j) is visible exactly when i and j are
less than L and j is at most i. The Boolean mask returned by
`dm::nn::causal_padding_keep_mask` broadcasts over attention heads.

The softmax normalizes over visible keys. An empty row has zero weights
and produces a zero context vector. This convention covers every query in
the zero-length item and prevents padded query, key, and value positions
from receiving a gradient from the attention loss.

> Run the three-length fixture

The TensorFlow fixture uses deterministic sine and cosine inputs. This
program keeps the same shapes and input values rounded to Float32, then
uses Float64 for the finite-difference check. Each panel uses the same
probability scale. Gray cells are excluded by the keep mask.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/attention_masks.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

int main() {
    namespace nn = dm::nn;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    constexpr int width = 5;
    const std::vector<int> lengths{5, 3, 0};
    const auto mask = nn::causal_padding_keep_mask(nn::from_vector(lengths), width);

    std::vector<double> q(45), k(45), v(30);
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < q.size(); ++i) {
        q[i] = static_cast<float>(std::sin(.23 * i));
        k[i] = static_cast<float>(std::cos(.41 * i));
    }
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < v.size(); ++i)
        v[i] = static_cast<float>(std::sin(.61 * i));
    const std::vector<nn::Tensor> inputs{
        nn::from_vector(q, {3, 1, width, 3}).requires_grad_(),
        nn::from_vector(k, {3, 1, width, 3}).requires_grad_(),
        nn::from_vector(v, {3, 1, width, 2}).requires_grad_()
    };
    const auto attend = [&](const auto& x) {
        return nn::scaled_dot_product_attention(x[0], x[1], x[2], mask);
    };
    const auto loss = [&](const auto& x) {
        const auto context = attend(x).output;
        return nn::sum(context * context);
    };
    const auto attended = attend(inputs);
    const auto gradients = nn::grad(loss(inputs), inputs);
    const auto check = nn::gradcheck(loss, inputs, {.atol = 1e-8, .rtol = 1e-6});
    if (!check.ok) throw std::runtime_error(check.message);

    auto plots = g::RLayout::create(1, 3).size(1050, 345);
    const std::vector<double> positions{0, 1, 2, 3, 4};
    auto palette = g::viridis_colors(64);
    palette.insert(palette.begin(), {226, 229, 233});
    for (int sample = 0; sample < 3; ++sample) {
        const int length = lengths[sample];
        std::vector<std::vector<double>> cells(width, std::vector<double>(width, -1));
        for (int query = 0; query < width; ++query) {
            double mass = 0;
            for (int key = 0; key < width; ++key) {
                const double probability = attended.weights.at({sample, 0, query, key});
                mass += probability;
                if (query < length && key <= query) cells[key][query] = probability;
                else if (probability != 0) throw std::runtime_error("Excluded key has weight");
            }
            if (std::abs(mass - (query < length ? 1.0 : 0.0)) > 1e-12)
                throw std::runtime_error("Attention probabilities do not have the expected mass");
            if (query < length) continue;
            const std::vector<nn::Tensor> padded{
                attended.output, gradients[0], gradients[1], gradients[2]
            };
            for (const auto& tensor : padded)
                for (int feature = 0; feature < tensor.size(-1); ++feature)
                    if (tensor.at({sample, 0, query, feature}) != 0)
                        throw std::runtime_error("Padding changed the context or gradient");
        }
        auto plot = g::RPlot::create().title(std::format("Valid length {}", length))
            .x_label("Key").y_label("Query");
        plot.x_ticks(positions, {"0", "1", "2", "3", "4"});
        plot.y_ticks(positions, {"0", "1", "2", "3", "4"});
        plot.x_limits(-.5, 4.5).y_limits(-.5, 4.5).image(positions, positions, cells, palette, -1.0 / 63, 1);
        plots.add(plot);
    }
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    plots.save_svg("build/attention_masks.svg");
    nn::save_npz("build/attention_masks.npz", {
        {"weights", attended.weights}, {"context", attended.output},
        {"dq", gradients[0]}, {"dk", gradients[1]}, {"dv", gradients[2]}
    });
    std::print("Valid rows sum to 1. All padded contexts and input gradients are zero.\n\n");
    std::print("Maximum finite-difference error across 120 input derivatives: {:.2e}.\n",
               check.max_abs_error);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Valid rows sum to 1. All padded contexts and input gradients are zero.

Maximum finite-difference error across 120 input derivatives: 4.93e-10.
\image(figures/attention_masks.svg)
// result_end

The item of length zero has no visible keys or queries. In the length-three
item, even large padding values cannot affect the context at a valid query.
The derivative check applies to the sum of squared context values and
includes valid and padded elements of Q, K and V.
